Subject: [PATCH] [M156] [Blink] Zero-initialize ImageDataBuffer readback
 buffer

FlyWeb pending: from branch-heads/8078 7ec583a50d. Applied after pendiente/chromium/0006; applies cleanly (identical diff). brave-core has chromium_src/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/graphics/image_data_buffer.h, which only adds a pixmap accessor for canvas farbling and does not touch the buffer allocation; no brave-core patches for these files.

Original change's description:
> [Blink] Zero-initialize ImageDataBuffer readback buffer
>
> ImageDataBuffer::ImageDataBuffer(scoped_refptr<StaticBitmapImage>)
> allocates its destination buffer via SkData::MakeUninitialized() before
> calling PaintImage::readPixels(). For a texture-backed PaintImage,
> readPixels() delegates to MailboxTextureBacking::readPixels() ->
> RasterImplementation::ReadbackImagePixels(). Because
> kDisableErrorHandlingForReadback is enabled by default [1], a failed GPU
> readback returns true without writing to the destination buffer, causing
> ImageDataBuffer to retain uninitialized heap memory.
>
> Switch ImageDataBuffer to SkData::MakeZeroInitialized(), matching other
> readback callers such as MailboxTextureBacking::GetSkImageViaReadback()
> [2] and StaticBitmapImage::CopyImageData() [3].
>
> [1] https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:gpu/command_buffer/client/raster_implementation.cc;l=1687-1690;drc=fa6817d43c5acec58ae2a0ed17dcf0e793290d36
> [2] https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/platform/graphics/mailbox_texture_backing.cc;l=69-70;drc=fa6817d43c5acec58ae2a0ed17dcf0e793290d36
> [3] https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/platform/graphics/static_bitmap_image.cc;l=62;drc=fa6817d43c5acec58ae2a0ed17dcf0e793290d36
>
